#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:101
msgid "The field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:103
msgid "How the NIF/CIF/NIE field looks on the billing and shipping forms. Leave any of these boxes empty and the field falls back to the default value shown in grey. The first two boxes leave this screen as soon as you switch the VIES VAT number or the EORI number on: from then on the label of that number is the one in use, for every customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:104
msgid "the name the customer reads above the field. NIF/CIF/NIE by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:105
msgid "the hint shown inside the empty field. NIF/CIF/NIE number by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:106
msgid "what the customer reads when the number is not valid. Please enter a valid NIF/CIF/NIE. by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:107
msgid "where the field sits in the form: the lower the number, the higher it goes. It is 31 by default, which places it right after the company name. The screen lists the priorities your other fields are using, so you can pick a number that puts it where you want."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:112
msgid "When it is required"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:114
msgid "Which forms show the field and when the customer is forced to fill it in. Billing and shipping are set separately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:115
msgid "the order cannot be placed without a number on the billing form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:116
msgid "makes the billing field required only for orders of that amount or more, taxes included, even when the box above is unticked. Leave it empty to switch it off. It never affects the shipping form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:117
msgid "the same, for the shipping form. It only has an effect when the field is shown there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:118
msgid "adds the field to the shipping form as well. Unticked, the field exists only on the billing form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:123
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:125
msgid "Whether the number is checked before the order goes through, or simply stored as typed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:126
msgid "checks that the number is a real NIF, CIF or NIE, letter included, and stops the order with the error message above if it is not. Unticked, anything the customer types is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:131
msgid "VIES VAT number"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:133
msgid "Lets customers from the rest of the European Union enter their VAT number, which is checked live against the VIES register of the European Commission. It needs the SoapClient PHP class: without it the plugin warns you and keeps this switched off. With the EORI number switched on as well, the two boxes that set the label leave this screen, because the EORI ones take over."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:134
msgid "switches the VAT number on. The four settings below only matter once it is ticked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:135
msgid "the label the whole field takes, for every customer and not only those outside your country, as soon as the VIES VAT number is switched on. NIF/CIF/NIE/VAT number by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:136
msgid "the hint inside that field, also NIF/CIF/NIE/VAT number by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:137
msgid "what the customer reads when VIES answers that the number does not exist. Please enter a valid VIES VAT number. by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:138
msgid "what the customer reads when VIES cannot answer because the shop has made too many requests in a short time. This is not a wrong number: it is the register asking you to wait."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:143
msgid "EORI number"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:145
msgid "The number customs uses to identify a business that imports or exports. Useful for shops that sell to companies outside the European Union."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:146
msgid "switches the EORI number on. The four settings below only matter once it is ticked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:147
msgid "the countries whose customers are asked for an EORI number. Leave the list empty and no country is asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:148
msgid "the label the whole field takes as soon as the EORI number is switched on, over the VIES one when both are on. NIF/CIF/NIE/EORI number by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:149
msgid "the hint inside that field, also NIF/CIF/NIE/EORI number by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:150
msgid "what the customer reads when the EORI number is not valid. Please enter a valid EORI number. by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:155
msgid "Tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:157
msgid "A one-off repair for shops that come from an older version of the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-nif-help.php:158
msgid "removes the duplicated billing_nif and shipping_nif rows that older versions of the plugin left behind on orders placed through Checkout Blocks. You only need it if your shop took orders that way before updating, it can be run as many times as you like, and on a shop with many orders it takes a while."
msgstr ""

